{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeTowerWitnessStrict","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeTowerWitnessStrict","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.MathlibExt.HeckeTowerWitness","lean:module:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeColimitFaithful"],"declarations":6,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeTowerWitnessStrict.twH_lt_succ","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeTowerWitnessStrict.twH_lt_succ","kind":"theorem","line":161,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeTowerWitnessStrict.lean#L161-L182","doc":"**The presented tower's filtration grows strictly at every level.**\n\nThis is what `HeckeTowerWitness`'s module docstring flags as unproved beyond\nlevel 0: `twH_mono` is `≤`, and `twH_zero_lt_one` covers only `H 0 < H 1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeTowerWitnessStrict.towerToColimit_twGen","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeTowerWitnessStrict.towerToColimit_twGen","kind":"theorem","line":155,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeTowerWitnessStrict.lean#L155-L157","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeTowerWitnessStrict.towerToColimit","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeTowerWitnessStrict.towerToColimit","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeTowerWitnessStrict.lean#L133-L152","doc":"**The presented tower's realisation at the Hecke parameter.**\n\nGenerator-for-generator, not collapsed: `twGen m ↦ g m`.  All three presented\nrelations hold in the colimit with matching indices. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeTowerWitnessStrict.gLim_notMem_H","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeTowerWitnessStrict.gLim_notMem_H","kind":"theorem","line":115,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeTowerWitnessStrict.lean#L115-L129","doc":"**The new generator is genuinely new.**\n\n`H_lt_succ` gives strictness without a witness; with `H_le_adjoin_gLim` the\nwitness is `g n` itself. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeTowerWitnessStrict.H_le_adjoin_gLim","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeTowerWitnessStrict.H_le_adjoin_gLim","kind":"theorem","line":94,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeTowerWitnessStrict.lean#L94-L113","doc":"**The colimit filtration is generated by the colimit generators.** ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeTowerWitnessStrict.eq_of_braid_of_comm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SchurWeyl.HeckeTowerWitnessStrict.eq_of_braid_of_comm","kind":"theorem","line":76,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/SchurWeyl/HeckeTowerWitnessStrict.lean#L76-L89","doc":"**In a commutative ring the braid relation forces adjacent generators to be\nequal.**\n\n`b·a·b = a·b·a` becomes `a·b² = b·a²`; substituting the quadratic on each side\nturns it into `h·a·b + a = h·a·b + b`.  So any commutative target of the presented\ntower identifies `σ_m` with `σ_{m+1}`, hence all generators by chaining, hence\nmaps every stage of the filtration onto the same subalgebra.  **No commutative\nalgebra separates `twH n` from `twH (n+1)`** — of any rank, product or not.  This\nis why `collapse` into the rank-2 `Hecke2` cannot be repaired by enlarging the\ntarget, and why the separator below is the non-commutative colimit. ","signatureChunk":0}]}